A||N||3||Eric_PA||Power drain on 84||||1||
Z||000000||Eric_PA||02-02-2001||06:55 AM||||I am having trouble with my 84 Fiero. It's a 4 speed with no options. Every once in a while when it's parked it will drain the battery. I thought it was maybe the headlight motors so I disconnected them this didn't help. I checked for trunk lights interier lights to be left on. Didn't find anything. I bought a new battery for it thinking it was that. I check voltage while running, I get 14.1 Volts so it's charging. Any ideas or sources that could drain the battery? Also this doesn't happen all of the time, it's random.<BR>Thanks<BR>Eric||||reg||1
Z||000001||William Federle||02-02-2001||08:28 AM||||I had a similar problem once with a 1988 Huyndai. It turned out to be the alternator.<BR>The voltage regulator in it was conducting to ground (slightly). I thought of it when I did something that I shouldn't have - I charged the battery with both cables still connected. The alternator got really warm. The problem went away when I replaced it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rodrv6||02-02-2001||05:06 PM||||I agree with William.  My 84 did exactly the same thing.  Turned out the alternator had a shorted diode.  I discovered the problem after the car had been parked overnight and I reached around the back of the alternator to check the power lead and the alternator was warm!!<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||1
Z||000003||RNGCRSH||02-03-2001||10:43 AM||||Mine had the same problem. I traced the problem to the Cigarette lighter, It seems that cigarette ashes will act as a resistor and slowly drain a battery. In my car the drain was about 1 Amp constant(battery would die overnight). I took the cigarette lighter out and tapped it on the ground to clean it out and have had no problems since. <P>I have aso heard of coins or silver chewing gum rappers getting in there and causing the same drian on the battery. <p>[This message has been edited by RNGCRSH (edited 02-03-2001).]||||reg||1
